<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Birnin Kebbi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Birnin Kebbi is a town in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, a capital of the Hausa Kingdom of Kebbi from the 16th century. Its walls protected the kingdom founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammadu-kanta">Muhammadu Kanta</a>, but in 1805 it fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fulani-war">Fulani jihad</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usman-dan-fodio">Usman dan Fodio</a>, and Kebbi's rulers continued their resistance from Argungu. It is today the capital of Kebbi State.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/birnin-kebbi.jpg" alt="Birnin Kebbi" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Faruku rama · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Central_masjid_birnin_kebbi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
